{
  "schema": "orfs.performance.gc-scaling.v1",
  "method": "For each (GOGC, GOMEMLIMIT) configuration: init a fresh volume, mount it with --direct-io and --profile-dir, drive it with cmd/orfsrw (N concurrent 4 KiB random readers + M concurrent writers), then SIGTERM the daemon so it writes runtime-metrics.json (runtime/metrics + /proc VmRSS/VmHWM) and pprof profiles. The driver measures application latency; the daemon measures the Go runtime.",
  "note": "BOUNDED sweep: 9 arms (each GOGC value at unlimited GOMEMLIMIT, plus the GOMEMLIMIT axis and the GOGC=off bounded cells); this is not the full 5x3 cross product. Each arm runs a fixed, short workload inside a 2 GiB / 4 CPU container. rss_bytes is REAL resident memory (VmRSS); peak_rss_bytes is VmHWM. gc pause percentiles come from the windowed /sched/pauses/total/gc:seconds histogram (bucket edges). alloc_bytes_per_s is /gc/heap/allocs:bytes over the daemon window. mutex_wait_seconds is the windowed /sync/mutex/wait/total:seconds. An arm whose daemon was OOM-killed (GC disabled with no memory limit) is recorded status=daemon_died, not given a fabricated number.",
  "bounded": true,
